      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Continuing Success</strong><br>\nFollowing the success of \"La Bohème,\" Puccini created other major operas, including \"Tosca\" (1900) and \"Madama Butterfly\" (1904). His operas are renowned for their intense drama and intricate musical portrayal of characters and emotions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Musical Style and Innovation</strong><br>\nPuccini's music combines the traditional elements of Italian opera with new influences, including verismo, a style focused on the realism of everyday life. His compositions are characterized by long, flowing melodic lines and a keen sense for orchestration and theatrics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The 'Trittico' and 'Turandot'</strong><br>\nPuccini's later works include \"Il trittico\"—a collection of three one-act operas—and \"Turandot,\" which was left incomplete at his death and later finished by Franco Alfano. \"Turandot\" contains one of opera's most famous arias, \"Nessun dorma.\"</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
