          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Personal Life and Challenges</strong><br>\nPuccini's personal life was marked by passionate relationships and a near-fatal car accident in 1903. Despite these challenges, he continued to compose and remained a dominant figure in the world of opera throughout his life.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Twilight Years and World War I</strong><br>\nDuring World War I, Puccini faced personal and health challenges, which impacted his work. However, he remained a patriot and supported Italian efforts during the conflict, although the war slowed the production and popularity of his operas.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nGiacomo Puccini died on November 29, 1924, from complications of throat cancer. His death marked the end of an era in Italian opera, but his works continue to be performed worldwide. His ability to touch human emotions through music ensures his enduring legacy as one of opera's greatest composers.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
